# Canonicalizes commit author/committer identity for display (git log,
# git shortlog, git blame, GitHub's contributors view). Does NOT rewrite
# history — the underlying commit objects and hashes are unchanged; this
# only remaps how existing identities are shown.
#
# Early commits used a personal name + personal email, and a batch of
# early commits used the bare `root` account on the deploy host (exposing
# the server's hostname). Both are remapped here to the same canonical,
# non-identifying project identity already used for later commits.
